{%- comment -%}
  snippets/kj-mark.liquid
  {% render 'kj-mark' %}                        → the KJ ellipse mark
  {% render 'kj-mark', mark: 'lada' %}          → the Lada script wordmark
  {% render 'kj-mark', mark: 'lada', label: 'Lada by Khan Jee' %}

  THE viewBox AND fill BELONG HERE, NOT IN THE DEFS.

  kj-svg-defs stores the KJ mark as a bare <path id="kj-path"> inside
  <defs>. A <path> carries no coordinate system and no fill of its own,
  so both have to come from the <svg> that instances it. Leave the
  viewBox off and the path draws at its native 1021x617 user units
  inside a 44px box — you see the top-left corner and nothing else.
  Leave the fill off and it paints black, so the mark stays black on the
  dark hero where it is supposed to be white.

  Both of those shipped once. Do not "simplify" them away again.

  The Lada mark is the client's own artwork (assets/lada-mark.webp), so
  it is an <img>, not an SVG path. It has a metallic gold gradient, which
  currentColor cannot express — any attempt to recolour it would flatten
  the thing that makes it the mark. It was supplied on a black card and
  has been keyed to real transparency, so it composites over the hero
  photograph as well as over the flat dark grounds.

  Because it is a fixed-colour image it must only ever be placed on a
  dark ground. Gold on white is around 2:1, which is why nothing puts it
  on the white surfaces.

  The lockup already reads "BY KHAN JEE", so do not set that line as
  text next to it.

  Colour comes from currentColor: set it on the parent, never here.
  Pass label to give the mark an accessible name; omit it and the mark
  is decorative, which is right when readable text sits beside it.
  Pass sizes on the Lada mark to tell it how wide its box really is.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign m = mark | default: 'kj'
-%}

{%- if m == 'lada' -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    THE CALLER HAS TO SAY HOW WIDE THE BOX IS, because the sections that
    draw this mark disagree by a factor of four and one <img> gets one
    sizes:

      lada-gateway crest   clamp(84px,10vw,124px)
      lada-band            clamp(210px,38vw,360px)
      hero-slideshow slide clamp(200px,32vw,400px)

    The crest is the one that matters: it is the largest thing painted
    on /pages/lada, which makes it that page's LCP, and it is fetching
    600px of artwork to fill 124. The two smaller renders below exist
    for it. Pass sizes: '(min-width:1240px) 124px, 10vw' there.

    The default is the widest of the three rather than the smallest, so
    a caller that says nothing wastes some bytes instead of painting a
    soft mark at 400px. Wrong-but-sharp beats wrong-and-blurry.

    The full 600px file stays as the top candidate: w520 is only 20%
    smaller, so there is nothing to gain by dropping it and a retina
    hero would have to upscale without it.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign mark_sizes = sizes | default: '(min-width:1250px) 400px, (min-width:625px) 32vw, 200px' -%}
  <img class="kj-mark kj-mark--lada{% if class %} {{ class }}{% endif %}"
       src="{{ 'lada-mark.webp' | asset_url }}"
       srcset="{{ 'lada-mark-w260.webp' | asset_url }} 260w,
               {{ 'lada-mark-w520.webp' | asset_url }} 520w,
               {{ 'lada-mark.webp' | asset_url }} 600w"
       sizes="{{ mark_sizes }}"
       width="600" height="447" decoding="async"
       {% if loading %}loading="{{ loading }}"{% else %}loading="lazy"{% endif %}
       {% if label %}alt="{{ label | escape }}"{% else %}alt="" aria-hidden="true"{% endif %}>
{%- else -%}
  <svg class="kj-mark kj-mark--kj{% if class %} {{ class }}{% endif %}"
       viewBox="0 0 1021 617" fill="currentColor"
       {% if label %}role="img" aria-label="{{ label | escape }}"{% else %}aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"{% endif %}>
    <use href="#kj-path"></use>
  </svg>
{%- endif -%}
